    "description": "What: an engine's heat at night (CE-4658, thermal drivers TD-S2; docs/designs/thermal/DESIGN_Thermal_Drivers.md \u00a74e). On basic-desert at 00:30 local, clear sky, two pairs 4 km apart so neither sees the other: 'Observer Idle' at (0, 0) watches 'Idling Tank' (a crewed T-72, its engine idling: a crewed vehicle starts Idle) 600 m east; 'Observer Parked' at (0, 4000) watches 'Parked Tank' (the same T-72, authored HeatSource Off: parked, engine cold) 600 m east. Both observers are the thermal observer (TKB 215: a hand-held thermal sight 1500 m, resolving a signature >= 0.3; their eyes reach ~125 m at night, their ears 750 m but a standing tank makes no sound). Judge: Observer Idle remembers his tank (an idling engine reads 0.2 + 0.4 x 0.8 = 0.52); Observer Parked never does (a cold hull reads its base 0.2). Both tanks keep the state they started with (HeatSource Idle / Off). Fail: the parked tank is seen, or the idling one is not.",
